Negative control for ONE sort source of truth (`P1-R9` · `R6-6`).

Hands the header click back to TanStack's own toggle, which keeps every OTHER
entry of the sort state in place. With the module's `-default,email` boot order
that turns "order by email address" into `order=-default,-email` from a header and
`order=-email` from the toolbar — the same intent, two different wire orders.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the sort-parity spec — a header and the toolbar control emit the same model
for the same intent.

